cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ANCOVA Ops in research, teaching, demos, or derived work, please cite this software."
title: "ANCOVA Ops"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cheng"
    given-names: "Gigi"
version: "0.6.0"
date-released: 2026-08-20
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gigichengnc/ancova-ops"
url: "https://github.com/gigichengnc/ancova-ops"
abstract: >-
  ANCOVA Ops is a reproducible research/software prototype for human-centred
  service operations. It converts unstructured service requests into explainable
  routing recommendations, preserves human review and audit history, records
  outcomes, and provides an evidence-aware evaluation layer with applicability
  checks, downstream regression/ANCOVA, offline policy research, and leakage-aware
  longitudinal benchmarks. Current quantitative evidence is synthetic or
  hand-authored development evidence and does not establish real-world service
  improvement or production readiness.
keywords:
  - "service operations"
  - "human-in-the-loop"
  - "ANCOVA"
  - "regression"
  - "offline policy evaluation"
  - "longitudinal analysis"
  - "data governance"
  - "responsible AI"
